    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Initiation 6 — Renegotiate.</strong> When one of your manifestations would misfire, you may instead accept a GM-set narrative debt (a future scene, a future cost, a future favor owed) and treat the manifestation as having succeeded at base tier. The debt is real; the GM's table runs the bill.</p>\n<p style=\"opacity:0.7;font-size:0.85em\">Discipline: passive Concurrency unchanged from Init 1; Renegotiate itself is a narrative reaction resolved at the table when a misfire would land.</p><div data-ft-per-use=\"1\" data-ft-per-use-key=\"pkInit6\" style=\"margin-top:0.7rem;padding:0.55rem 0.75rem;border:1px solid #b08acc;border-radius:0.35rem;background:rgba(70,55,95,0.18);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.78rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#d4b8e8;margin-bottom:0.25rem\">⟁ Per-Use Ability — <strong>Renegotiate</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.86rem;opacity:0.92;line-height:1.4\"><strong>Recovery:</strong> Unlimited (debt-bound) &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Action:</strong> Reaction (on misfire) &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Use:</strong> Click this feature on your sheet to invoke.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.82rem;opacity:0.85;margin-top:0.3rem\">When one of your manifestations would misfire, accept a GM-set narrative debt and treat the manifestation as having succeeded at base tier. The debt is real — the GM's table runs the bill.</div>\n</div>",
